        "githubCommitMessage": "perf(db): stop lobby polling from hidden tabs\n\nThe game lobbies each ran a fixed-interval poll (3s, or POLL_MS) that kept\nfiring from backgrounded tabs. A hidden tab cannot be sitting in a lobby —\nnobody picks an opponent or sees a list they are not looking at — so those\nticks were pure Postgres reads that nothing consumed, and they scale with\nhow long players leave the lobby open rather than with games actually\nplayed.\n\nSwap every lobby poll onto the shared startVisibleInterval helper, so the\ntimer only runs while the tab is visible and returning to it refreshes\nimmediately instead of waiting out a stale interval. It is the non-hook\nhelper from the polling module because these effects declare their poll\ncallback locally, which keeps each change a two-line swap rather than an\neffect restructure.\n\nCovers mini-golf, tic-tac-toe, sudoku-duel, four-in-a-row, dots-and-boxes,\nlane-runner, memory-grid, keno, mines-pvp, rps, uno, tower-arena, precision,\nplus pool-masters' two polls (lobby list and the created-lobby w",
