        "githubCommitMessage": "feat(moderation): keep profane names and fake reviews off the public surfaces\n\nNames and reviews are what a visitor reads before signing up, and both were\nreachable with junk: a profane Clerk username flowed straight onto the\nleaderboard, and a hand-seeded \"Test review\" row was sitting approved on\n/reviews credited to a \"Verified player\". Neither is a job for the report\nqueue — the second was approved on purpose — so the rule moves to the write\nand read paths themselves.\n\nNames are filtered everywhere one is written (the user.created webhook,\nsync-user, profile rename) and replaced with a deterministic clean handle\ninstead of failing the signup. The public review read path refuses\nplaceholder rows outright, with migration 0194 deleting the ones already\nlive. The home leaderboard, the classement page and the review wall can flag\na name or a review in place, and the admin queue now shows the flagged review\nand can hand the player a fresh handle without banning anyone. A one-off\nsweep (scripts/purge-profaned-use",
